Name     cap23-9;
PartNo   00;
Date     2026-01-01;
Revision 01;
Designer decpld;
Company  decpld;
Assembly none;
Location none;
Device   g22v10;

/* EXPECT refusal

   Nine independent product terms on pin 23, whose block owns one
   output-enable row and eight data rows. A sum of nine distinct single
   literals is already minimal SOP, so CUPL cannot merge them into
   eight.

   `cap23-8` is the same design one term smaller and compiles, which is
   what makes this a measured boundary rather than a transcription of
   the datasheet's Figure 1-1. run.sh reads the marker above, reports
   the refusal as a result, and fails loudly if the oracle ever accepts
   this design -- an acceptance would mean the block map is wrong.
*/

PIN 1 = i0;
PIN 2 = i1;
PIN 3 = i2;
PIN 4 = i3;
PIN 5 = i4;
PIN 6 = i5;
PIN 7 = i6;
PIN 8 = i7;
PIN 9 = i8;
PIN 23 = o0;

o0 = i0 # i1 # i2 # i3 # i4 # i5 # i6 # i7 # i8;
